    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Objective</h2>
        <p>This level is for <strong>verification</strong> and <strong>reflection</strong>. Students do not write new code.</p>
        <p>They must play the game to completion (collect the 4 key items, open the airlock, defeat the boss, and escape).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Key Items & Locations</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <ul style="list-style-type: none; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">🔑 <strong>Command Keycard</strong>: Hidden in <em>Command Centre</em> (Interact with panel).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">🔋 <strong>Control Cell</strong>: In <em>Research Lab</em>.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">🔧 <strong>Crowbar</strong>: In <em>Main Corridor</em> or Maintenance (used to open Supply Closet).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">🔦 <strong>Flashlight</strong>: In <em>Maintenance</em> (Needed for dark rooms).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">💾 <strong>Data Chip</strong>: In <em>Research Lab</em> (Allows non-violent boss win).</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">The Boss Fight</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>Option A: Combat</strong></p>
            <p>Attack the Security Chief. He has 55 HP and 3 Armour. Need a good weapon (Plasma Cutter in Armoury) and Med Patches.</p>
            
            <p><strong>Option B: Tech Solution (Non-Violent)</strong></p>
            <p>If they found the <strong>Data Chip</strong>, they can choose "Use Item" -> "Data Chip" in combat to disable him instantly.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Verification Checklist</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: check;">
            <li>✅ Player has name and class descriptive text.</li>
            <li>✅ Inventory limits (10 items) work.</li>
            <li>✅ Items can be used (healing/buffs).</li>
            <li>✅ NPCs respond to dialogue choice.</li>
            <li>✅ Combat loop works (Attack/Damage).</li>
            <li>✅ Save/Load restores exactly the same state.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

